  "id": "multidirectional-manual-core-hold",
  "name": "Multidirectional Manual Core Hold",
  "definition": "A standing bilateral isometric core family in which an athlete extends clasped hands and maintains the trunk and pelvis while a partner applies changing-direction manual perturbations through the hands. The perturbations create flexion, lateral-flexion, and rotation tendencies that the athlete resists without producing repetitions. Partner force is intentionally not recorded as a numeric load because the source does not quantify it. The product classifies the fixture as bodyweight to suppress a false resistance field; the required partner remains explicit in the name, variant, and instructions rather than being misrepresented as measurable equipment. Fixed-direction presses, partner wrestling drills, steady band or cable Pallof holds, and moving trunk exercises remain outside this contract.",
