      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand with both feet about hip-width apart, soften the hips and knees, brace the trunk, and extend both arms near shoulder height with the hands clasped. Have a partner place their hands against yours.",
        "movement": "Keep the hands, trunk, pelvis, and feet as still as possible while the partner applies brief pressure from changing directions.",
        "endpoint": "Continue resisting the changing pushes for the set time without turning the drill into a movement repetition.",
        "controlledJoints": "Maintain the arm lever and resist trunk flexion, side bending, and rotation without stepping.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Keep both feet planted and use only enough partner pressure to preserve a controlled neutral position.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": [
          "Stepping or lifting a foot changes the two-foot standing fixture.",
          "Allowing repeated trunk bending or turning changes the task from an isometric hold to a dynamic drill.",
